scenario a receiver that loses its fix keeps its last coordinate on the wire
describe The position field of a GNSS frame is not emptied when the solution
describe goes away. The receiver keeps sending the coordinate it last solved
describe for, with a fix type of `none` in the same frame saying there is no
describe position at all — so the frame arrives looking exactly like an answer,
describe once a second, for as long as the dropout lasts.
describe
describe This trace is that frame meeting the OTHER provider. The wearer walks
describe away from where the fix was lost; the node still has a receiver and
describe reports where they actually are. Those two are not in conflict — only
describe one of them is claiming to know anything — and a device that reports
describe `provider-disagreement` here is telling its wearer that its two
describe sources contradict each other when one of them has stopped answering.
describe
describe The dropout is the ordinary case, not the exotic one: a doorway, a
describe canopy, a wrist turned away from the sky. Found by the review of
describe `6965191..8d757a7`, issue #178.

at 0
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect validity valid
  expect trust trusted

# The fix goes. The coordinate does not: still 0.5°N 1.0°E, and `acc` is
# retained along with it, because a field nobody rewrote keeps its old value.
# `fix-lost` is the honest reason and it weighs 20 — below `degrade_at`, so it
# says "no position" without also saying "somebody is lying".
at 6000
  fix none
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  expect validity nofix
  expect reason fix-lost
  expect trust trusted

# The node, half a kilometre north, with a fix of its own. That is where the
# wearer now is. Our own last real measurement was taken six seconds ago, which
# is outside the comparison window, so there is nothing here to compare it
# with — and the retained coordinate is not a substitute for one.
at 6500
  fix 3d
  pos 5045000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 6000
  sats 9 12
  provider other
  expect no-reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust trusted

at 7000
  fix none
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  expect validity nofix
  expect reason fix-lost

# And again a second later, which is the half that outlives one frame: a
# retained coordinate does not refresh anything, so this does not become a
# fresh answer by being repeated. Before the fix each of these frames restamped
# the local side of the comparison with its arrival time, and the disagreement
# was renewed for the whole dropout rather than for one epoch.
at 7500
  fix 3d
  pos 5045000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 6000
  sats 9 12
  provider other
  expect no-reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust trusted

# Half a minute of it.
at 30000
  fix none
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  expect validity nofix
  expect reason fix-lost
  expect trust trusted

at 30500
  fix 3d
  pos 5045000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 6000
  sats 9 12
  provider other
  expect no-reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust trusted

# The sky opens and the receiver solves again — at the node's position, because
# that is where this device has been for half a minute. Five hundred metres over
# thirty-one seconds is 16 m/s, which is a bus, not a teleport.
at 31000
  fix 3d
  pos 5045000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect validity valid
  expect no-reason fix-lost
  expect no-reason position-jump
  expect trust trusted

# The comparison reopens with it. This one agrees, and the agreement is a real
# one: both sides measured a position within the window.
at 31500
  fix 3d
  pos 5045000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 6000
  sats 9 12
  provider other
  expect no-reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust trusted

# And a real disagreement is still reported. The gate was shut for the dropout,
# not for the session — a device that stopped comparing after its first dropout
# would have thrown the second source away for the rest of the boot.
at 32000
  fix 3d
  pos 5090000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 6000
  sats 9 12
  provider other
  expect reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust degraded
